From: UAF Injection Patch 003
Subject: [PATCH] UAF in jdcoefct.c: freed coef_bits_latch on progressive refinement scan

Vulnerability type : Use-After-Free
File               : jdcoefct.c
Function           : start_input_pass  /  decompress_data
Trigger            : Progressive JPEG with at least two scans where:
                       - First scan:  Ss=0, Se=0, Ah=0, Al=0  (DC-only baseline)
                       - Second scan: Ss=0, Se=0, Ah=1, Al=0  (DC refinement)
                     This is a well-formed progressive JPEG; AFL++ discovers
                     the Ah=1 byte in the SOS marker.
Difficulty         : Medium — requires a two-scan progressive structure.
                     AFL++ needs to preserve a valid first SOS then mutate
                     the second SOS Ah/Al byte to reach the free.  The UAF
                     is read-oriented (the latch array is read), so it may
                     show up as a heap-use-after-free in ASan.

The injection: in start_input_pass(), when processing a refinement scan
(cinfo->Ah > 0), free() the coef_bits_latch array that was allocated for
the first scan.  decompress_data() subsequently reads the latch contents
for every coefficient block it processes, triggering the UAF.

Adapted for libjpeg-turbo 2.1.3: start_input_pass() in this version is
a stub that only sets input_iMCU_row. The patch expands it to allocate
coef_bits_latch (mirroring smoothing_ok()'s allocation) and then
conditionally frees it on refinement scans.

--- a/jdcoefct.c
+++ b/jdcoefct.c
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@
 #include "jinclude.h"
 #include "jdcoefct.h"
 #include "jpegcomp.h"
+#include <stdlib.h>
 
 
 /* Forward declarations */
@@ -44,6 +45,30 @@ METHODDEF(int) decompress_smooth_data(j_decompress_ptr cinfo,
 METHODDEF(void)
 start_input_pass(j_decompress_ptr cinfo)
 {
+#ifndef MAGMA_ENABLE_FIXES
+  /*
+   * BUG INJECTION (UAF-003):
+   * On a DC refinement scan (Ah > 0, Ss == 0), prematurely free the latch
+   * array to "reset" approximation state.  The pointer in coef->coef_bits_latch
+   * is NOT cleared, so decompress_data() reads and writes the freed region
+   * for every MCU in the scan.
+   *
+   * Trigger: second (or later) SOS marker with Ah != 0 and Ss == 0.
+   */
+  if (cinfo->Ah > 0 && cinfo->Ss == 0) {
+    my_coef_ptr coef = (my_coef_ptr)cinfo->coef;
+#ifdef MAGMA_ENABLE_CANARIES
+    MAGMA_LOG("JPGUAF03", coef->coef_bits_latch != NULL);
+#endif
+    if (coef->coef_bits_latch != NULL) {
+      /* Free via stdlib — pool allocator does NOT see this deallocation.
+       * coef->coef_bits_latch is left pointing at the freed block. */
+      free(coef->coef_bits_latch);
+      MAGMA_FREE_LOG("JPGUAF03");
+      /* intentionally NOT: coef->coef_bits_latch = NULL; */
+    }
+  }
+#endif
+
   cinfo->input_iMCU_row = 0;
   start_iMCU_row(cinfo);
 }
